<title>USA: TABLE-Schultz Sav-O Stores Q2 net income up.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Schultz Sav-O Stores Q2 net income up.</headline>
<dateline>SHEBOYGAN, Wis. 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>1997			1996</p>
<p> Shr			   $0.37		    $0.33</p>
<p> Net			  $1,791		   $1,576</p>
<p> Revs		     $109,844		 $105,544</p>
<p> Avg shrs		    4,799		    4,752</p>
<p>			    6 Months</p>
<p> Shr			  $0.70		    $0.59</p>
<p> Net			 $3,378		   $2,837</p>
<p> Revs		    $248,670		 $239,623</p>
<p> Avg shrs		   4,830		    4,770</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: -- Company says takes two charges in first half amounting to  $0.12 a share. First pre-tax charge to operations of $700,000 for  projected expenses to terminate an underperforming franchise operation.   Second pre-tax charge to operations of $275,000 was recorded in Q1  when management decided to terminate its Springtime bottling operations.  Company says entered into arrangements with independent private label  vendors for future production.</p>
</text>
